WEBVTT

00:02.460 --> 00:04.340
<i>Our first race
in the playoffs was...</i>

00:04.550 --> 00:06.130
<i>a complete disaster.</i>

00:07.010 --> 00:10.720
<i>To avoid a second disaster,
I made a deal with Prince Aikka.</i>

00:11.010 --> 00:13.810
<i>No weapons, a race for speed.</i>

00:15.470 --> 00:18.850
<i>I had to do some drastic things
to keep my promise.</i>

00:21.730 --> 00:24.480
<i>And then everything
became a big</i> mess.

00:25.030 --> 00:26.690
<i>I don't know what's next.</i>

00:26.820 --> 00:30.450
<i>To be honest, I'm not sure
I can take this anymore.</i>

01:49.650 --> 01:52.450
Go away.
I said I wasn't coming out.

01:57.530 --> 02:00.700
Molly, I know we've had
differences of opinion,

02:00.950 --> 02:02.460
specially in the last race.

02:02.580 --> 02:05.750
But we have found ourselves
at a critical point in the selections.

02:05.920 --> 02:08.090
And we must think
of the team first.

02:09.710 --> 02:13.340
I think now is a good time
to get together, and talk things over.

02:13.510 --> 02:14.380
Wrong!

02:14.550 --> 02:17.140
Now is a good time
to stay in my room.

02:21.810 --> 02:23.940
I guess we'll move on
to plan B, then.

02:30.320 --> 02:33.150
All you do is take, Don Wei.
You give 0.

02:34.360 --> 02:37.530
You don't deserve
a loving daughter like me.

02:38.120 --> 02:40.200
And I don't deserve
a father like you!

02:40.740 --> 02:41.950
I said get lost!

02:48.090 --> 02:50.380
Oh, Rick, I'm so sorry.

02:50.710 --> 02:51.760
I thought you were...

02:52.090 --> 02:54.170
Yeah, I know
who you thought I was.

02:54.300 --> 02:56.930
Get dressed, little mouse.
School is in session.

02:57.220 --> 02:58.890
Huh? What do you mean?

02:59.390 --> 03:01.100
I'm your new coach, kiddo.

03:01.850 --> 03:03.350
Leave me alone!

03:06.060 --> 03:07.850
I'm not in the mood.

03:09.900 --> 03:12.030
Help! I'm being hijacked!

03:12.400 --> 03:14.820
-No!
-Molly's in good hands now.

03:15.320 --> 03:16.860
Help!

03:18.870 --> 03:20.280
What's going on?

03:20.450 --> 03:23.080
The long delayed
taming of the shrew.

03:25.620 --> 03:28.130
Why does she get
to have all the fun?

03:33.760 --> 03:35.590
In case you hadn't realized <i>it...</i>

03:35.800 --> 03:38.090
our next race is not a marathon.

03:44.890 --> 03:47.230
What's the big idea
about refusing to race?

03:47.640 --> 03:49.690
I never came here to race.

03:49.860 --> 03:52.820
And the team
never trusted me anyway.

03:53.440 --> 03:54.860
Trust you?

03:55.690 --> 03:57.490
I'll be the judge of that.

03:59.660 --> 04:01.530
Pick up the pace, slowpoke.

04:08.420 --> 04:10.460
Oh, great. They're bonding.

04:10.790 --> 04:12.130
Huh! Whatever.

04:19.550 --> 04:22.180
Look at this dress.
It's made for you.

04:22.600 --> 04:24.680
Get lost.
I'm trying to be sad.

04:26.520 --> 04:28.350
Well, hello there.

04:28.980 --> 04:31.350
If it isn't
my good friend Jordan.

04:32.980 --> 04:34.570
You're not training
with your partner?

04:34.730 --> 04:37.110
What partner?
You think I've got a partner?

04:37.280 --> 04:39.530
I sure hope
your team recovers quickly

04:39.700 --> 04:41.700
from its two crushing defeats.

04:43.530 --> 04:45.200
How did you...

04:46.290 --> 04:49.250
I've heard the name
of your next adversary.

04:49.920 --> 04:51.710
He's one of the best
in the competition,

04:51.880 --> 04:54.960
and very aptly named...
Super-Racer!

04:58.420 --> 04:59.930
Well, my bags are packed.

05:00.090 --> 05:03.090
With three defeats under our belt,
we can go home early.

05:03.350 --> 05:06.470
Hey, Super-Racer is
nothing to make fun of.

05:06.720 --> 05:07.770
I've seen him race.

05:08.020 --> 05:09.060
He's fearless.

05:10.060 --> 05:10.850
Aikka.

05:11.140 --> 05:12.270
Oh, yes.

05:12.440 --> 05:15.440
He's a living legend,
this Super-Racer.

05:15.610 --> 05:17.400
Unbeatable.

05:18.030 --> 05:19.740
This is all your fault.

05:20.070 --> 05:21.360
What's my fault?

05:25.030 --> 05:27.450
<i>Eh ! Regarde un peu
m': tu vas, idiot!</i>

05:27.660 --> 05:30.290
Humans are always
so unpredictable.

05:30.540 --> 05:31.920
And so rude, too.

05:54.400 --> 05:56.770
Don't even think
about disappearing.

06:13.580 --> 06:14.580
Not bad.

06:18.130 --> 06:19.050
For a girl.

06:20.380 --> 06:22.470
-Ready for another go?
-Are you kidding?

06:22.630 --> 06:25.590
I've been running in circles
around that stupid pool for hours.

06:25.760 --> 06:27.390
Don't worry. It gets better.

06:27.550 --> 06:29.560
Soon you won't
even feel the pain.

06:29.850 --> 06:31.310
Whatever.

06:32.350 --> 06:33.730
Go get 'em, tiger!

07:05.930 --> 07:07.220
Colonel Toros!

07:07.970 --> 07:10.600
What are you so desperate
to speak to me about, Toros?

07:10.890 --> 07:14.770
I was concerned that my young ally
was becoming a bit soft.

07:15.640 --> 07:17.060
So the rumors are true.

07:17.230 --> 07:19.690
Prince Aikka
is in the Crogs' pocket.

07:23.690 --> 07:25.990
I doubt your father
would be pleased to learn

07:26.150 --> 07:28.070
of your actions
in the last race,

07:28.240 --> 07:31.080
risking defeat
for the sake of an Earth girl.

07:31.370 --> 07:32.990
You know I won that race.

07:33.580 --> 07:35.710
It was a good thing you did.

07:35.870 --> 07:37.830
I was starting to wonder
if the Nourasians

07:38.000 --> 07:39.790
had found new allies.

07:40.170 --> 07:42.920
Alliance does not
mean servitude, Toros.

07:43.090 --> 07:47.300
<i>We have our own agenda,
not the Grog agenda.</i>

07:47.470 --> 07:49.890
And I am determined
to win the Ultimate Prize.

07:50.510 --> 07:52.890
You are still young, Aikka.

07:53.850 --> 07:55.680
You have much to learn.

08:02.820 --> 08:05.740
I wish you the best
on your coming race, Prince.

08:05.990 --> 08:09.070
And don't forget to answer
the call of the Crogs,

08:09.240 --> 08:10.820
whenever it may come.

08:20.750 --> 08:22.250
The call of the Crogs.

08:22.880 --> 08:24.960
If only Molly could see this.

08:34.430 --> 08:36.060
Hello, Prince.

08:36.220 --> 08:38.690
You and I have some
unfinished business.

08:38.850 --> 08:39.770
Oh really?

08:39.940 --> 08:42.770
Breaking your word was not enough?
Now you must spy?

08:44.070 --> 08:47.440
Stay away from Molly.
Or I promise you you'll regret it.

08:48.280 --> 08:49.990
Says who? Her guardian?

08:50.610 --> 08:52.280
Says her partner.

08:56.700 --> 08:58.830
I suggest you leave
while you still can.

09:13.140 --> 09:15.640
You know, I've been waiting
a long time for this.

09:35.200 --> 09:37.200
That was pathetic. Try again.

09:37.370 --> 09:39.450
OK, but this is the last time.

09:42.120 --> 09:43.630
To achieve perfect balance,

09:43.790 --> 09:47.090
you must become
one breathing entity with the pole.

09:53.800 --> 09:56.600
I had a feeling that control
was not your strong suit.

09:56.810 --> 09:58.470
We'll try an easy one.

10:00.270 --> 10:02.060
This is going to hurt.

10:10.740 --> 10:13.280
<i>One breathing entity.</i>

10:37.510 --> 10:40.140
Now there you go,
not bad at all.

10:42.060 --> 10:43.060
What's next?

10:48.400 --> 10:51.650
Molly, you've got
good technique, good speed,

10:51.820 --> 10:53.240
and great reflexes.

10:53.570 --> 10:54.900
Why aren't you doing better?

10:55.110 --> 10:56.530
I'm doing my best.

10:56.700 --> 10:58.490
I'm just a girl, remember?

11:00.160 --> 11:02.040
Don't play that game with me.

11:02.200 --> 11:05.710
You're a star-racer pilot,
a pilot for the Earth team.

11:07.960 --> 11:09.340
What's holding you back?

11:18.260 --> 11:20.140
Nothing's holding me back.

11:20.680 --> 11:24.270
You know, it's motivation
that gets you across the finish line.

11:24.430 --> 11:27.020
Why did you join the team
in the first place?

11:35.150 --> 11:38.030
OK, then, Molly.
Why do you race?

11:50.790 --> 11:52.500
I do it for my father.

11:53.050 --> 11:55.010
Finally,
we're getting somewhere.

11:55.220 --> 11:58.130
I'm sure back on Earth,
he thinks about you every day.

11:58.470 --> 12:00.680
He has no idea
how much I do for him.

12:01.010 --> 12:03.600
I think coming here
was a big mistake.

12:05.310 --> 12:08.940
Listen, Molly, it's no mistake
that you're here.

12:09.350 --> 12:11.560
Without you, the Earth team
would be finished.

12:13.570 --> 12:16.280
Anyway, this race
is the greatest ever.

12:16.440 --> 12:19.160
Isn't that worth giving it
your best shot?

12:28.540 --> 12:29.960
Then quit slacking off.

12:40.800 --> 12:43.640
What this ship needs
is a little TLC.

12:46.430 --> 12:48.270
Why don't you see
what you can do?

12:48.850 --> 12:51.020
It might even
improve your spirits.

12:52.270 --> 12:55.190
-Are you sure?
-Sure I'm sure.

12:57.400 --> 13:00.240
Think of it
as your last exercise for today.

13:05.910 --> 13:06.700
Yeah.

13:07.080 --> 13:09.210
Here goes nothing.

13:14.790 --> 13:15.880
That hurts.

13:18.760 --> 13:20.220
What happened to your face?

13:20.630 --> 13:23.140
I fell, choking on a pretzel.

13:23.260 --> 13:24.720
Hey, about what happened...

13:26.100 --> 13:27.020
Let's go.

13:34.360 --> 13:37.440
Next, we call forth
the Earth team!

13:39.190 --> 13:41.070
Let's hope your training pays off.

13:41.490 --> 13:44.450
You know, Don, a little faith
might do some good.

13:51.160 --> 13:53.620
What is that monstrosity?

13:53.960 --> 13:56.210
It looks like
a rabbit's head to me.

13:56.630 --> 14:00.010
Hey, you wanted me
to light a fire, so I lit a fire.

14:00.210 --> 14:03.930
Remember, before I met you,
Don, I didn't have any tattoos.

14:06.800 --> 14:10.430
And now, without further delay,
I call forth...

14:11.350 --> 14:12.690
Super-Racer!

14:23.650 --> 14:26.700
Give it up for Super-Racer!

14:32.080 --> 14:34.370
I see you tried to top
the fabulous design

14:34.540 --> 14:36.000
of my super star-racer.

14:36.330 --> 14:37.840
Your attempt has failed!

14:38.000 --> 14:40.090
That voice sounds
really familiar.

14:40.340 --> 14:43.300
Satis, what are you doing
in that silly costume?

14:43.670 --> 14:46.050
Safis?
What are you talking about?

14:46.220 --> 14:51.350
I am... Super... Racer!

14:54.230 --> 14:56.350
Go on, giggle all you want.

14:56.520 --> 14:59.480
In a few minutes,
I'll be the one laughing...

14:59.940 --> 15:01.780
When you're losing the race.

15:02.820 --> 15:05.320
Don't let his dubious appearance
fool you, Molly.

15:05.490 --> 15:07.570
Super-Racer is one victory
ahead of us.

15:07.740 --> 15:09.280
He's only lost to Toros.

15:09.780 --> 15:13.120
This guy cannot be for real.
Come on. He looks like...

15:13.450 --> 15:15.710
Losing this race would mean...

15:17.250 --> 15:19.750
<i>...the end of the world
as we know it.</i>

15:21.210 --> 15:24.470
We need this victory,
do you hear me?

15:47.450 --> 15:49.450
Let's see how well
you trained today.

15:56.830 --> 15:58.670
Back off, you super wacko.

16:03.420 --> 16:06.920
Looks like these kids have something
up their sleeves... after all.

16:16.730 --> 16:18.190
They had better not blow it.

16:20.560 --> 16:23.110
Time to teach them
a lesson of my own.

16:40.830 --> 16:42.880
Molly, we may have
a problem back here.

16:49.930 --> 16:51.550
-Lose him!
-I'm trying, sir.

16:51.720 --> 16:53.100
But I'm at maximum speed.

16:53.390 --> 16:55.520
He's got a bigger wingspan, Molly.

16:55.680 --> 16:57.810
He's not as maneuverable
as the Arrow 2.

16:58.350 --> 17:00.020
Take advantage of that.

17:10.030 --> 17:11.030
Not good.

17:23.880 --> 17:25.920
You've done well so far,
young Molly.

17:26.130 --> 17:29.630
But are you truly worthy
of winning the Ultimate Prize?

17:35.560 --> 17:36.810
Molly!

17:37.180 --> 17:38.100
Disaster.

17:46.980 --> 17:48.530
What's up with the controls?

17:49.240 --> 17:49.990
Not a word.

17:50.280 --> 17:52.610
She must not lose
her concentration.

17:58.950 --> 18:01.460
Stick with me, Jordan.
We're going after him.

18:12.300 --> 18:14.760
That's it.
No one touches my turret.

18:26.770 --> 18:28.190
Hey, no hitchhikers!

18:33.740 --> 18:34.490
Jordan!

18:34.990 --> 18:37.120
I don't need a clean,
thank you.

18:42.290 --> 18:42.960
No!

18:44.330 --> 18:45.540
Molly! What are you doing?

18:45.920 --> 18:47.420
Something you wouldn't understand.

18:47.540 --> 18:49.590
-I'm going back for someone.
-Molly.

18:49.880 --> 18:53.550
Jordan wouldn't have wanted you
to lose this race. Think about it.

18:54.220 --> 18:56.010
For once, I agree with Don.

18:56.220 --> 18:58.430
The track's rescue team
is on the way.

18:58.600 --> 19:01.470
The best thing you can do
for Jordan is to beat this guy.

19:20.410 --> 19:23.660
If you can't beat me here,
you won't stand a chance on Oban.

19:26.370 --> 19:28.960
Impossible.
She'll never make it.

19:38.890 --> 19:41.180
<i>One breathing entity.</i>

19:48.060 --> 19:49.400
Here goes nothing!

20:03.160 --> 20:03.790
What?

20:12.550 --> 20:16.470
And so the torch is passed
to a new generation.

20:21.100 --> 20:25.060
The winner, the Earth team.

20:28.480 --> 20:29.310
Where is she going?

20:43.450 --> 20:44.620
Jordan!

21:04.600 --> 21:07.930
Another reckless gamble,
but I'll take the victory.

21:11.060 --> 21:13.360
There was nothing reckless
about that race.

21:13.520 --> 21:15.780
And you know it
better than anyone.
